Z||000006||fierodave||08-20-2001||10:46 PM||||Thanks Guys! but I am only the messenger  here lol<BR>I Guess I should have been a little clearer on the Imsa Fiero!<BR>it was built on a 85 southern GT chassis, with A/C cruise tilt delay power windows,locks & Mirrors about 8 years ago. <P>It was never finished, and from being moved from storage place to storage place and a few different owners, It never did get finished <P>It was slightly damaged and was never fully completed!  <BR>I picked it up and sent it to the body shop right away! was just going to get the glass work done and into primer for a new owner to finish, But I did a trade and the new owner wanted it with a show ready paint job, So I set it up and that is where we are at now.  I sold this car last year before my Ca. Trips to a good friend out in Merced Ca.  He now has some serious health issues to address, so he may not be able to take delivery on the car!<P>I will handle the sale for him if he in fact he decides not to get the car. The car has just had all the glass work and a $2,500+ Paint job was done by MD Classic auto Restorations in Wi.  It was a side job and was just completed!  <P>As soon as I have all the details I will share them! along with a price if it does come up for sale.  <BR>It's a project car though, and still needs work: brakes need some work from sitting, sail windows replaced, headliner. Fluids changed, tune-up,  But the most costly part is done-  The glass and paint work!<BR>Thanks for looking  I hope to know more by the weeks end!<P>Regards,<BR>Dave Andregg<BR>  <P><p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||1
